From bd00943c7bfae04d5044921b70a44758a5f204db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:03:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore and JavaScriptCore: no Web Inspector on the Amiga
 port

The Amiga port has no inspector frontend, local or remote, but the
inspector was still compiled and linked: about 2.8 MB of the engine.
Under PLATFORM(AMIGA) WebCore leaves inspector/ and its bindings out of
the build, and JavaScriptCore keeps only what the console uses (console
messages, their arguments and call stacks). InspectorInstrumentation
returns at once, Page, LocalFrame and worker global scopes have no
inspector controllers, canvas calls are never traced, and the heap has
no subspaces for the injected script host or inspector call frames.
Console messages still reach the ChromeClient.

Team 3
